          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. The Ashoka Chakra has 24 spokes. What is the degree measure of the angle between two spokes next to each other? What is the largest acute angle formed between two spokes?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.753,
            0.122,
            0.878,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.753,
                0.122,
                0.878,
                0.216
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_41_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.212,
            0.737,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Puzzle:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " I am an acute angle. If you double my"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.232,
            0.236,
            0.886,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "measure, you get an acute angle. If you triple my measure, you will get an acute angle again. If you quadruple (four times) my measure, you will get an acute angle yet again! But if you multiply my measure by 5, you will get an obtuse angle measure. What are the possibilities for my measure?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.424,
            0.376,
            0.63,
            0.402
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Summary"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.429,
            0.812,
            0.45
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "point",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " determines a location. It is denoted by a capital letter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.453,
            0.884,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "line segment",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " corresponds to the shortest distance between two points. The line segment joining points S and T is denoted by ST."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.501,
            0.885,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "line",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is obtained when a line segment like ST is extended on both sides indefinitely; it is denoted by ST or sometimes by a single small letter like m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.574,
            0.884,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ray",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a portion of a line starting at a point D and going in one direction indefinitely. It is denoted by DP where P is another point on the ray."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.622,
            0.885,
            0.714
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "An angle can be visualised as two rays starting from a common starting point. Two rays OP and OM form the angle ∠POM (also called ∠MOP); here, O is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "vertex",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the angle, and the rays OP and OM are called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "arms",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the angle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.717,
            0.884,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The size of an angle is the amount of rotation or turn needed about the vertex to rotate one ray of the angle onto the other ray of the angle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.766,
            0.885,
            0.81
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The sizes of angles can be measured in "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "degrees",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". One full rotation or turn is considered as 360 degrees and denoted as 360°."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.814,
            0.835,
            0.834
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Degree measures of angles can be measured using a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "protractor",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.838,
            0.885,
            0.906
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Angles can be "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "straight",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (180°), "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "right",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (90°), "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "acute",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (more than 0° and less than 90°), "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "obtuse",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (more than 90° and less than 180°), and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "reflex",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (more than 180° and less than 360°)."
            }
          ]
        },
